――A sudden, radical shift in the circumstances surrounding Kugelschreiber Castle.

Hearing it from Tiga's own lips, Subaru and the others caught their breath.

The castle had traversed space—which meant, in other words, that it had broken out of its hidden pocket dimension and returned to the surface world for the first time in centuries.

Except――

"Looks like your side didn't see this coming either."

"――. Well, who knows? Could be a ploy on our part to make you think that, couldn't it? Trusting too much in what you see is a bad habit of yours, my friend. I've been telling you that since way back, haven't I?"

"Subaru-sama, a wind of untruth is..."

"Shh! Crusch, shh! We're in the middle of high-level psychological warfare here!"

"Sloppy, sloppy. I'm not falling for that. ...Though I'll admit, being told I've forgotten something does make my heart skip a beat."

Having gauged Subaru and the others' reactions, Tiga glanced to Subaru's side—at Melty, who stood there, still watching him.

The gaze she fixed on Tiga was meaningful, thick with expectation and heat. The fact that she had called him by name left no doubt that there was some connection between the two.

"And kinda seems like you've got something going on too... 'Black Dog', care to share your history with that little spirit?"

"Not a sin-gle shred, not a damn thing, I don't remember any of it at aaaaall! Blame it on some teeny spirit I've never laid eyes on — sorry, so so sorry, I'm sor-ry!"

"...Right, gotcha, don't worry."

Just like Melty, 'Black Dog' had some history too—apparently an extraordinary connection with the squirrel-like spirit glaring from Tiga's shoulder. Despite his typical flippant act, Subaru's two months of experience told him he probably wasn't lying.

Truth be told, the sheer amount of information being crammed into his head was making it spin, but with Bellaris—the one who had actually been making his head spin—now silenced, he had no excuse to stop thinking. ――Right now, their fighting force consisted of an energetic 'Black Dog' and a somewhat energetic Crusch, along with the half-dead trio of Subaru, Ferris, and Melty. Even the first two were worn out and wounded, far from top condition; reckless moves were strictly forbidden.

Still, it wasn't as if there was no hope on their side. And to make that hope come up――

"Now then, there's five of us, and even counting that little spirit on your shoulder, there's only two of you. By the numbers, we've got you beat by more than double. Total advantage. If you're gonna surrender, now's your chance."

"...Must've heard that wrong, yeah? He's completely ignorin' how banged up they are and talkin' to us like that just 'cause of the numbers, yeah."

"You didn't hear wrong, Pooka. That's just the kind of guy my friend is. Well, even I'm surprised he managed to totally disregard their exhaustion, though."

"And you've got more of the seriously wounded. That's another point in our favor."

"You say that with so much swagger despite the hole in your back, it almost makes me wanna believe it."

Shrugging with not the slightest intention of buying it, Tiga clearly had zero talent for acting. At the very least, learning that the squirrel-like spirit's name was Pooka, and confirming that the enemy was willing to chat, were solid gains.

Even so, in the face of this overtime small talk that couldn't possibly be called a negotiation, the fighting spirit of Crusch and 'Black Dog' slowly mounted, naturally sensing that a clash was unavoidable――

"――tch! What're you wastiiin' time chattin' for?! Do 'em in, do it alreadyyy! Cut 'em dowwwwn, 'Executor'! Ain't that what you're heeeere for?!"

However, the one who grew impatient with the situation and cried out, even more than Subaru and the others, was Reborn.

Leaning on his half-shears for support, Reborn had lost his sight to Crusch's sword strike, rendering him unable to use the power of 'Silence' which depended on his vision. Even so, he barked at Tiga, relying purely on presence, imploring him to fulfill the duty that had brought him here.

At that plea, Subaru ran his tongue over his dry lips, cursing the interference.

"...No lie, shutting up and fighting is the worst-case scenario."

Even if the restraints of 'Silence' and 'Ring Finger' had lifted, allowing Subaru's tongue and brain to operate normally, that alone wouldn't bridge the decisive gap in combat power.

While the foul play of pairing 'Cor Leonis' with 'Blue' let them support the fight, how long that could hold out was an absolute gamble.

That was why Tiga pressing them with brute force was the last thing they needed――

"Hurryyy up and take out these――"

"――Tornel, I know you can hear me. Put 'Detour' at full strength. We're falling back."

"Wha...t?!"

Yet Tiga's next words betrayed both Subaru's dread and Reborn's plea.

Having given his order to the absent third 'Beloved Child' by name, Tiga spun on the spot and closed the distance with Reborn, whose blood-soaked face was turned toward him. Then, he brought the pommel of his drawn scimitar down hard against the back of Reborn's neck as he stood frozen.

"Guh."

"Told you. Time's up. Besides, it's your own fault for jumping the gun without waiting for orders."

The dwarfish frame collapsed with a short groan, and Tiga tossed it lightly over his shoulder with a dismissive remark. Then, looking back at the dumbfounded party,

"You heard me. We're retreating, and taking the brat with us. That's it for today."

"Whoa, whoa, whoa, ain't that a mighty selfish way of puttin' it? Barging in out of nowhere, droppin' riddles, and then just takin' off? Leave your life and your answers behind, why doncha!"

"Wh-What vulgar, savage barkin', yeah...! I can't believe for a second someone like that's my contractor, yeah! You tricked me, yeah?!"

"Like hell I know or care, dummy! Burn to cinders carryin' that dead weight! Burning!"

Capping off the quarrel at the top of his lungs, 'Black Dog' thrust his palm forward, unleashing a raging inferno.

The green flames swept horizontally like the breath of a Dragon, robbing Tiga and the indignant spirit on his shoulder of any avenue of escape. Confronted with this unimaginable outrage, Subaru nearly screamed out a "You id—!", but an even louder voice rang out from Melty beside him.

Except, it wasn't a scream.

"No! Fire doesn't work on Pooka!"

"Huuuh?!"

At her confident shout, 'Black Dog' raised a suspicious growl. And the truth of her words was proven the very next moment, as the green blaze reached Tiga and the others—and was swallowed head-on.

Right in the center of the surging green flames, the exact portion colliding with Tiga and his companions was cleanly bitten away, vanishing. The one responsible was Pooka, licking her lips.

Wiping her mouth lightly with a front paw, the adorable-looking spirit spoke.

"Seems like that girl knows what's what, yeah. ――That I'm the Great Spirit of Fire."

"If you knew, you should've said somethin'! What, showin' off your wicked-woman charm here? Never miss a beat to self-promote, huh?!"

"'Black Dog' attacked out of nowhere, that's why! More importantly――"

Snapping back against 'Black Dog's' unfair accusation, Melty's eyes darted past the parted flames toward Tiga. Taking that as his cue, Tiga leapt nimbly backward with Reborn in tow—and scooped up the collapsed Bellaris with his outstretched arm.

"Still alive, right? Spread 'Ring Finger'. Don't hold back. ――Doesn't work on me anyway."

"...O-Oh my? Does that mean... you trust me, that you... love me? I love you too...!"

Just how tough was she? At Tiga's words, Bellaris shamelessly responded with love. Drifting in right after was a sweet scent that inflamed the mind and robbed it of sanity.

Bellaris's 'Ring Finger' activated, and once more, the component that breached emotions flooded the air.

"Ferris! I'm about to go crazy, hit me with that cure—yoo-hoo!"

"――gh, you already are! Don't move, stop thrashing! I can't treat you!"

Shouldering the mental afflictions of every ally through the power of 'Cor Leonis', Subaru triggered the combo of having Ferris treat him, somehow digging his heels in. Yet even amidst that scramble, Tiga, holding the two defeated 'Beloved Children' like sacks of grain, aimed to disengage from the battlefield.

Crusch and 'Black Dog' moved separately to intercept, but――

"I won't let you get in the way, yeah!"

"――!"

Puffing her cheeks, Pooka roared, spitting back the very flames of 'Black Dog' she had just consumed.

The green inferno bore down on the two trying to pursue Tiga. Crusch severed the wave with an upward slash, stepped past the curtain of fire—and violently collided with 'Black Dog'.

"Eek?!" "Whoa?!" Their startled cries overlapped as the unexpected impact sent both tumbling to the floor. It wasn't a repeat of infighting caused by 'Ring Finger'—it was something else.

"――Why?! Where'd Tiga go?!"

Beyond the tripped-up Crusch and her companion, Subaru had lost sight of Tiga as well.

It happened right after Pooka's expelled flames momentarily blocked their vision, obscuring Tiga and the others. Having lost track of the person who should have been right there, Subaru doubted his own eyes. But he wasn't the only one who had lost him. Even Ferris, pressed close at Subaru's side despite his missing arms, blinked in utter confusion, muttering, "Huh? Huh?"

Subaru could feel Ferris's healing power closer than anything else. Meaning, this wasn't the influence of Bellaris's 'Ring Finger'――

"――'Detour'! So it doesn't just make you lose your way?!"

The 'Detour' that had separated their team in the castle and made regrouping an ordeal—if that power, whose user had still not shown their face, could not only scramble a sense of direction but also disrupt cognitive faculties, then their gaze and awareness had been taken on a 'detour', causing them to lose sight of Tiga.

At this rate, Tiga would slip right past their awareness and escape, leaving them helpless――

"Wait!"

In that instant, Melty raised her slender voice, standing in his path with her staff in hand.

Catching a faint glimpse of her in the corner of his vision, Subaru forcibly tilted his head to resist 'Detour'. Melty stood before the door leading out of the basement, directly confronting the oncoming Tiga.

With both arms full carrying the two 'Beloved Children', Tiga's eyes sharpened.

"Get out of the way! You'll get hurt!"

"Then take responsibility if you hurt me!"

"What kind of logic is that?!"

At Melty's answer as she blocked the path, Tiga's eyes went wide with shock. The distance between them closed, and just when it seemed Melty was about to pay the price for her recklessness――

"Tch! Pooka!"

"Hold on tight to 'em, yeah!"

Summoned, Pooka leapt from Tiga's shoulder, swelling up in an instant from a twenty-centimeter size to a massive five meters. Her round tail grew proportionately, swinging to catch Tiga's back softly and launching him forward.

"――gh, Tiga!"

Flying in an arc, Tiga soared over the head of the wide-eyed Melty. She reflexively reached out her hand, but it couldn't reach him with his newfound momentum and height.

"See ya."

"Tiga—!!"

With only a fleeting meeting of their eyes, Tiga shot off like an arrow from his very first step on landing, leaving the frantically screaming Melty behind.

His feet didn't slow. 'Detour' wouldn't allow anyone to catch up to his retreating back.

"Wait! I said wait, Tiga! Tigaaa!"

No matter how many times she screamed, the voice wouldn't reach him, just as her outstretched hand couldn't.

The distance between them steadily opened, and eventually, the receding footsteps vanished. Behind him, the giant Pooka dissolved into particles of mana, disappearing as she pursued the fleeing Tiga.

"Damn it, they totally..."

They got away. ――That was the ending he couldn't bring himself to say out loud, and he had no choice but to accept it as the result of their clash with the 'Beloved Children' in Kugelschreiber Castle.

――With the intrusion of Tiga Rauleon and Pooka, the battle had reached a thoroughly ambiguous conclusion.

Honestly, there was no other way to put it: Tiga had played them. Putting the reliability of their info aside, if they had secured the two downed targets, they could have unraveled some of the secrets of the mysterious 'Beloved Children'. Even if that proved impossible, it would have whittled down the enemy's dangerous combat assets.

Yet all of that had gone down the drain with their retrieval.

"Still, if the fight had kept going, we're the ones who would've been in deep trouble. Never guessed Tiga was a spirit arts user. Totally fooled us."

"――. No, that's not it. Tiga isn't a spirit arts user. As far as I know, Pooka just stays with him, that's all..."

"Without a contract? So like Anastasia-san and Scarfidna, then? ...If that's the case, what kind of relationship do they have?"

"That... I'm sorry. I don't know. Only that it isn't a contractual one."

Clutching her collapsed staff, Melty's downward reply was vague. But to Subaru, that vagueness didn't stem from lies or evasion. Most likely, Melty truly didn't know the finer details of Tiga and Pooka's relationship.

However, when it came to herself and Tiga, that had to be a different story.

"――. I'll tell you everything later, I promise. But right now..."

"I know. Checking the situation with Kugelschreiber Castle and regrouping with Beako and the others comes first... Ferris! Your arms?! Are they gonna reattach properly?!"

"I'm concentrating right now, don't talk to me! I'm numbing the pain so my hands are shaking!"

"You say your hands are shaking, but the shaking hands are completely detached..."

Snapping back in a high-pitched voice, Ferris was in the middle of reattaching the arms pinned to the wall—his severed forearms from the elbows down—using healing magic.

Having his arms chopped off had been well outside Subaru's expectations, so if Ferris's arms didn't go back on, he'd have to spend the rest of his life taking responsibility. When he voiced something along those lines, Ferris had given him an utterly disgusted look, though.

"Besides, if anyone has to atone for a lifetime, I think it would be me, since I was the one who actually severed them."

"I feel pretty responsible for making you do it, too. How's your body holding up, Crusch?"

"No major injuries. I can still――"

Fight, she was probably about to say. Yet contrary to the will behind her words, her body couldn't keep up with Crusch's feelings. ――Her knees buckled, her form swaying. Subaru reflexively reached out, hurriedly catching her collapsing body.

"Whoa, careful! You okay?"

"Huh...? Subaru... sama..."

"It's gotta be the aftereffects of the 'Dragon's Eye'. You pushed yourself to the absolute limit, Crusch."

"But, I can still..."

"No, you can't push it. Rest for now. We'll pick up the slack. Mainly 'Black Dog', anyway."

Watching Crusch stir weakly, Subaru gave his answer, to which 'Black Dog' reacted with a disgruntled "Say whaaat?", but Subaru shut him up with a glare.

Reaching into Crusch's coat pocket, Subaru pulled out her eyepatch, gently slipping it over her heavy-lidded left eye.

"We'll talk when you wake up. About your heroic deeds and all that."

"――. Yes."

Nodding amidst her fading consciousness, the eye not covered by the patch closed as well.

Over these past two months, whenever she had to rely on the power of the 'Dragon's Eye', she had always looked stern and tense as she collapsed into an exhausted sleep. But looking at her sleeping face now, Subaru thought the edge had softened, bringing him a small measure of relief.

"――Subaru-kun."

As Subaru adjusted his hold on the sleeping Crusch, Ferris stood before him.

From the sleeves of his black suit, the once-lost arms were extended, his palms opening and closing to show off their recovery. Seeing that they were properly reconnected brought another sigh of relief.

"Honestly, it was so gruesome I couldn't look straight at it... but you can really heal back from that."

"Yep. If the severed parts are there and the person's Od hasn't forgotten its original state, I can pretty much heal it completely."

"Feels like you casually dropped something absurdly insane, but I'm just glad. ...Mind if I carry Crusch on my back? My hands are the most free right now."

"――Mm, thanks. I hate you."

"A dere-tsun femboy is way too fresh of a genre..."

As expected, a plan that relied on Ferris had severely tanked his approval rating. Considering his baseline was probably already low, it had likely swung straight into the negatives; Subaru was too terrified to ask.

Even so, repelling the 'Beloved Children' would have been impossible without Ferris, and without Crusch. There were plenty of emotional grievances, but it was an outcome they had wrenched away with everyone doing their utmost.

"Even if Tiga managed to put a damper on things in the end...!"

"U-Um, I'm sorry. I apologize on Tiga's behalf..."

"Hah! Acting like a goody-two-shoes, what's with 'on his behalf'?! Like that's gonna fill the void, the misery, as if! So, where do we go from here?"

"First off, stop picking on Melty-chan. Next, like I said—regrouping with Beako and the others takes priority. But we move carefully."

Though Tiga had retreated with the injured 'Beloved Children', the whereabouts of the third remained unknown, and there was a very real possibility of an ambush lurking in the castle. They knew far too little about this place to drop their guard and assume the threat was entirely repelled.

All the more so when the castle had apparently broken through to the surface world—thrusting itself above the clouds of the Lifaus Highway, gathering everyone's eyes.

"After all, they say this castle was built by Echidna. Knowing her, she wouldn't hesitate to pull some trial where we have to escape a hurtling castle before it crashes, just to test whoever broke in."

"What kind of perception is that? Isn't she Beatrice-chan's mother?"

"...A twisted-to-the-core personality that stops just barely short of a Sin Archbishop?"

Strictly speaking, in terms of sheer malice, she wasn't much different from a Sin Archbishop, but since she was already deceased and couldn't cause any more widespread damage, she got that much leeway. Though, considering Sphinx's rampage in the Vollachia Empire, depending on what sins she had kept hidden, that evaluation could crash through the floor at any moment.

Subaru looked around at his companions, each wearing a distasteful expression at his answer.

"Anyway, pay absolute attention to the floors and walls. If we're out of the pocket dimension, we probably won't be falling to our deaths forever, but..."

"――Ah, they say you don't gotta worry that much."

"————"

At that voice, which came almost out of nowhere, they spun around as if spring-loaded. They had had quite enough of new intruders, but their tension and dread proved unwarranted.

Poking his head out from the stairwell connecting the basement to the upper floors was a familiar face――

"――Rachins! You're safe!"

"'Don't just go throwin' my name around so casually,' is what I wanna say, but... you guys look completely beat to hell. Ain't this way worse than what I heard from the 'Librarian'?"

Scanning the battered group lined up in the basement, Rachins spoke. He had parted ways with them prior to the encounter with the 'Beloved Children'.

From the looks of it, unlike Subaru's group which had been through a continuous bloodbath, Rachins showed no signs of having been swept up in violence. It seemed he had luckily avoided crossing paths with the enemy, but――

"Where's Russell-san... 'Silver Fox'? Weren't you together?"

"He's safe—or, well, apparently it was the guy's read on things that kept the enemy from spottin' us. Just as we were headin' back to the entrance with the documents, the value of the entrance plummeted off a cliff or somethin'..."

"Value... the Divine Protection of Evaluation? It can be used like that...?"

His explanation basically meant that the value of the castle's entrance had crashed—that it had shifted from something useful to something hazardous for Russell, the bearer of the Divine Protection. If he could sense an anomaly at that point, then sure enough, avoiding the 'Beloved Children' might have been possible.

Truth be told, a warning would have been appreciated, but separated as they were, it couldn't be helped. Better to be glad that nothing irreparable had happened while Subaru and the others weren't there.

"I'd love to catch up, but 'Long Tongue'-kun, isn't it crazy outside?"

"Oh, right, that. Word is the castle shot out of the pocket dimension. It could be a 'Witch's' trap to round up and wipe out intruders. We have to, right now..."

"That ain't it. The one flyin' it is the 'Librarian', and 'Silver Fox' gave the order."

"――Beako and Russell-san did?"

Cut off in his panic, Subaru blinked in astonishment.

The unexpected report that Beatrice and Russell were doing something together was shocking enough, but even more so if it was something that tore away all secrecy, like making the castle fly.

From two months of working as a collaborator for the 'Six Tongues', it should have been self-evident that Russell hated drawing attention more than anything else.

"The two of them are safe, right? What were they thinking, making the castle fly? What were you doing, why didn't you stop them?"

"Don't go hittin' me with one question after another, you're loud as hell! If you're so curious, don't stand around gabbin' here, just go ask 'em directly."

"Guess you're right. Can we use 'Door Crossing'?"

"Yeah. That's how I popped over here too. Man, what a freaky spell."

With a remark that would have had Beatrice puffing her cheeks and stamping her feet had she heard it, Rachins began walking ahead to lead the way. Then, after his first few steps, he stopped, turning just his head back. "Oh, yeah, that's right."

"I'll answer just one of those questions from before... turnin' this castle into a stronghold, they said."

"Huh?"

"I'm givin' you the answer to what they were thinkin' when they made the castle fly. Makin' it our stronghold. ――If we're gonna take the Kingdom back for real, we can't keep runnin' and hidin' from place to place forever."

And with that, he revealed the reason why Russell, despite his hatred of flashiness, had sent the castle into the sky.
